      "writtenOn": "2022-12-16T20:18:58Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m not sure this is a good approach for a symbol that enables a library/subsystem.\n\nIt looks like upstream, symbols like `CONFIG_I2C` must be explicitly enabled and all the I2C controllers/drivers have a dependency on this symbol.\n\nI think we still want boards to explicitly enable RTC support, but the device drivers that provide RTC functionality can use DT_HAS_*_ENABLED.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 570,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 573,
        "endChar": 0
      },
      "revId": "c36b7af95bce1e9ca217153c49e1b1dc0d0f9a35",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "3753f253_bed67a79",
        "filename": "zephyr/Kconfig",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 573,
      "author": {
        "id": 1477788
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-01-02T17:35:36Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Right, the subsystem shouldn\u0027t be enabled like that. However I see that in the upstream they started to use the `select I2C` for devices that require the I2C. Should we start using that or continue to require manual enable of the subsystems and only use `default y` with dependency for subsystem?",
      "parentUuid": "802963ac_10acc44f",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 570,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 573,
        "endChar": 0
      },
      "revId": "c36b7af95bce1e9ca217153c49e1b1dc0d0f9a35",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
